#
# Counter-example for math:HomogeneousOperandDimensionedConstraint: a
# math:DimensionalExpression whose second math:homogeneousOperand is a
# math:MeasurableFunction (NOT a math:Quantity, so the math:Quantity-scoped
# math:hasDimension min-1 restriction never reaches it) that carries no
# math:hasDimension at all. The closed-world logic:Constraint
# ∀o,E: homogeneousOperand(E,o) → ∃d. hasDimension(o,d) then fails for that
# operand, so validation MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent
# (math:UndimensionedQuantity). The first operand IS dimensioned, so the
# expression still carries its required two math:homogeneousOperand (no
# math:MalformedDimension), and the reasoner-derived homogeneity law
# (dimEqual) never fires — its antecedent needs BOTH operands' dimensions
# bound, so an undimensioned operand yields no math:DimensionalInhomogeneity,
# isolating the single violation.
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecHomogeneousOperandUndimensioned).
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:mixedExpression a math:DimensionalExpression ;
    math:homogeneousOperand ex:dimensionedOperand , ex:undimensionedOperand .

ex:dimensionedOperand a math:Quantity ;
    math:hasDimension math:timeDimension .

ex:undimensionedOperand a math:MeasurableFunction .
